---
title: Associated Data and Media
sidebar:
  label: Associated data and media
  order: 7
---

Use `Associated Data` for specimen-linked digital files and external links that
are not specimen parts or media records—such as GenBank accessions,
MorphoSource records, analysis files, or external database URLs. It is the
storage-icon tab of the `Specimen Parts` card.

| Field | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `Data type` | `Link` or `File`. |
| `Name` | Source or dataset name, such as `GenBank` or `MorphoSource`. |
| `Description` | Accession number or short description of the data. |
| `Date` | Date associated with the data. |
| `URI` | External URL (with a valid scheme, such as `https://`) when `Data type` is `Link`. |
| File selector | Local non-media file attachment when `Data type` is `File`. Media files belong in `Media` below. |

{% steps %}

1. Open the storage-icon tab of the `Specimen Parts` card and select
   `Add associated data`.
2. Choose `Data type` (`Link` or `File`), then enter `Name`, `Description`,
   and `Date`.
3. Under `Resource`, enter the URL in `URI` for a `Link`, or select a file for
   a `File`. On desktop, choose `Copy to project` to store a managed copy with
   NAHPU, or `Link original` to point to the file in place; a linked original
   stops working if the file is moved or deleted.
4. Save the entry.

{% /steps %}

Use an entry's menu to `Edit`, `Show info`, `Share`, or open it (`Open link` or
`Open in default app` on desktop). Check linked files after a project transfer
and inspect any missing-file warning icon.

## Media

Use `Media` at the bottom of the specimen form for photos, video, and audio of
the specimen. Select `Add` to attach items using `Take photos/videos` (mobile),
`Record audio`, `Add from gallery` (mobile), or `Add from file`, or select
`Gallery` to browse the shared media gallery.

Open an item's menu and choose `Edit` to update its `File name`, `Caption`,
`Tag`, and `Photographer`. Media are stored once in NAHPU's shared media
library and linked to the specimen.
